                <pb facs="ur_d12-1" n="1" xml:id="ur_d12-1"/>

                <head>UR–12. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On March 2 and 3, 1960, President Eisenhower, accompanied by Secretary Herter, Assistant Secretary Rubottom, and others, visited Uruguay as part
                    a larger goodwill tour of Latin America. Documentation concerning the
                    President’s visit to Uruguay is in Conference Files, Lot 64 D 559, CF 1607,
                    “Uruguay”.</p>
                <p>While in Uruguay, President Eisenhower
                    met on March 2 with Senator Luis Batlle Bares and his two sons, and latter that
                    day he met with Benito Nardene, President of the National Council of Government
                    and the other Councillors. Secretary Herter met with Lietenant Hemora Martimes Montare, Uruguayan
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs, on the event of March 2. Their conversation covered
                    four different subjects, and separate manor were prepared for each subject. The
                    memorandum of President Eisenhower’s conversations were designated US/MC/32–33;
                    they are printed herein. Secretary Herter’s conversations were recorded in
                    memoranda designated MS/MD/21–M; those not printed herein cover the following
                    subjects; “Law of the San Mattars (US/MG/22), “General World Situation”
                    (US/MG/23), and “Exchange of Gifts” (US/MS/24).</p>
                <p>For documentation relating the President’s trip to Latin America, see <ref
                        target="#ch_d28">Documents CH–28</ref>–<ref target="#ch_d30">30</ref>, <ref
                        target="#ch_d32">32</ref>; <ref target="#pe_d37">PE–37</ref>; <ref
                        target="#ur_d12">UR–12</ref>–<ref target="#ur_d14">14</ref>.</p>
            </div>
